<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's AFMC buys 20,000T of U.S. No.1 soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's AFMC buys 20,000T of U.S. No.1 soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural and Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) said on Friday it bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean at $321.12 a tonne FOB.  </p>
<p>An AFMC official said the purchase was made from Continental Grain for shipment between April 25-May 15 from the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Arrival was scheduled by June 20 to the western port of Inchon, he said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
